 until August 15 at 5:45PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"At 336 PM MDT, Broadcast media reported flash flooding was occurring\nnear Chambers and Iliff, and Mississippi and Havana. Between 1.5 and\n3 inches of rain have fallen. Additional rainfall amounts up to 0.2\ninches are possible in the warned area. Flash flooding is already\noccurring.\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Heavy rain producing flash\nflooding.\n\nSOURCE...Broadcast media reported.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of creeks and streams,\nroads, and low lying areas.\n\nSome locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nEastern Denver, Aurora, and Buckley SFB.\n\nThis includes the following streams and drainages...\nToll Gate Creek, Sand Creek, Cherry Creek, South Platte River,\nFirst Creek, East Toll Gate Creek, West Toll Gate Creek, Murphy\nCreek, Coal Creek, Westerly Creek, Third Creek and Second Creek.","ends":"2026-08-15T17:45:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Adams, CO; Western Arapahoe, CO; Denver, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.0a3442297a267fb83636a62cc0b9d378cc47647b.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.0a3442297a267fb83636a62cc0b9d378cc47647b.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued August 15 at 11:52AM MDT until August 15 at 10:00PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"* WHAT...Flash Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is possible.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of central and northeast Colorado, including the\nfollowing areas: the southern Front Range Foothills, Palmer Divide\narea, I-25 corridor, and all of our eastern plains counties.\n\n* WHEN...Until 10 PM MDT this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\nFlooding may occur in poor drainage and urban areas.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Additional thunderstorms and heavy rainfall this afternoon,\ncombined with the heavy rainfall from the past 3 days, will bring\na threat for flash flooding this afternoon and evening. Stronger\nstorms will be capable of producing 1 to 2 inches of rain in 30\nminutes, with isolated areas receiving storm totals of 2 to 4\ninches.","ends":"2026-08-15T22:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Jefferson and West Douglas Counties Above  6000 Feet/Gilpin/Clear Creek/Northeast Park Counties Below 9000 Feet; Larimer County Below 6000 Feet/Northwest Weld County; Boulder And Jefferson Counties Below 6000 Feet/West Broomfield County; North Douglas County Below 6000 Feet/Denver/West Adams and Arapahoe Counties/East Broomfield County; Elbert/Central and East Douglas Counties Above 6000 Feet; Northeast Weld County; Central and South Weld County; Morgan County; Central and East Adams and Arapahoe Counties; North and Northeast Elbert County Below 6000 Feet/North Lincoln County; Southeast Elbert County Below 6000 Feet/South Lincoln County; Logan County; Washington County; Sedgwick County; Phillips County","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.eea7fe66bbe726127cab571e453d260029b0d72c.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.eea7fe66bbe726127cab571e453d260029b0d72c.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-15T19:12:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KBOU 151912 AFDBOU Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Denver/Boulder CO 112 PM MDT Sat Aug 15 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Another round of showers and thunderstorms this afternoon and evening. Heavy rainfall and flash flooding are the main threats today. A few thunderstorms could become severe, with strong winds and hail possible. - Monsoon moisture lasts through Sunday, brin","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-15T19:21:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Rest of today through Sunday... Moisture will remain high across the area today, as scattered to numerous showers and thunderstorms move through ag